l":"https://api.github.com/users/namelessman80/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namelessman80","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/namelessman80/advanced-customer-service-ai/commits/1d95f6961df6dc36c942ef0b28309ef48ff3444e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-08T03:37:58Z","email":"132729710+namelessman80@users.noreply.github.com","name":"namelessman80"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-08T03:37:58Z","email":"132729710+namelessman80@users.noreply.github.com","name":"namelessman80"},"message":"Fix flaky test_8: improve hallucination detection logic\n\nProblem: Test was too sensitive and failed intermittently when AI responses\ncontained words like ''temperature'' or ''weather'' in refusal statements.\n\nSolution:\n- Split hallucination keywords into ''strong'' and ''weak'' categories\n- Strong indicators (sunny, rainy, cloudy) always trigger failure\n- Weak indicators (temperature, degrees) only fail if no graceful refusal\n- Added better debugging output showing which keywords were detected\n\nTest now passes consistently (verified with 3 consecutive runs).\nReduces false positives while maintaining detection of actual hallucinations.","tree":{"sha":"9958c8f2e8e8bf4b9922732250277b6f26c00135","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/namelessman80/advanced-customer-service-ai/git/trees/9958c8f2e8e8bf4b9922732250277b6f26c00135"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/namelessman80/advanced-customer-service-ai/git/commits/1d95f6961df6dc36c942ef0b28309ef48ff3444e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132729710?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namelessman80/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namelessman80/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namelessman80/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"ht