ithm provides true uniform random distribution\n   - Users will now see much better variety in quiz questions\n\n2. Misleading question count - updated from \"100+\" to \"42\"\n   - Actual count: 42 questions in quiz-data.js\n   - Changed welcome screen statistic to reflect reality\n\nChanges:\n- quiz-data.js: Implemented shuffleArray() with Fisher-Yates algorithm\n- quiz-data.js: Updated getFilteredQuestions() to use new shuffle function\n- index.html: Changed question count from \"100+\" to \"42\"\n- index.html: Updated cache version quiz-data.js v=8 (was v=7)\n\nResult: Users will experience much better randomization and variety in quiz questions.","tree":{"sha":"16e600408e819bc6b7ec8b005a6be9894c5c8ce0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/trees/16e600408e819bc6b7ec8b005a6be9894c5c8ce0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/commits/4381646e47ca94525b4d88f74a9bfc353c802123","verification":{"payload":"tree 16e600408e819bc6b7ec8b005a6be9894c5c8ce0\nparent ebe355a0c415e9157794cbbb5763cdf49096c9b3\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762478651 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762478651 +0000\n\nFix quiz randomization and update question count\n\nProblems fixed:\n1. Poor randomization algorithm - replaced sort(Math.random) with Fisher-Yates shuffle\n   - Old: sort(() => 0.5 - Math.random()) gives biased distribution\n   - New: Fisher-Yates algorithm provides true uniform random distribution\n   - Users will now see much better variety in quiz questions\n\n2. Misleading question count - updated from \"100+\" to \"42\"\n   - Actual count: 42 questions in quiz-data.js\n   - Changed welcome screen statistic to reflect reality\n\nChanges:\n- quiz-data.js: Implemented shuffleArray() with Fisher-Yates algorithm\n- quiz-data.js: Updated getFilteredQuestions() to use new shuffle function\n- index.html: Changed question count from \"100+\" to \"42\"\n- index.html: Updated cache version quiz-data.js v=8 (wa