iew questions from top GitHub resources\n\nSources analyzed:\n- awesome-behavioral-interviews (behavioral patterns)\n- master-coding-interview (data structures & algorithms)\n- tech-interview-handbook (interview best practices)\n- ztm-master-the-coding-interview-ds-algo (coding patterns)\n- coding-interview-university (CS fundamentals)\n\nNew questions added (20 total with translations):\n\n**Big O & Complexity Analysis:**\n- Dynamic array amortized complexity O(1)\n- QuickSort average vs worst case O(n log n) vs O(n²)\n- BST vs Hash Table lookup comparison\n- MergeSort space complexity O(n)\n- Lowest Common Ancestor (LCA) time complexity O(n)\n\n**Data Structures:**\n- Hash Table advantages over arrays\n- Heap vs BST differences and use cases\n\n**Algorithms:**\n- Recursion vs Dynamic Programming (memoization vs tabulation)\n- BFS vs DFS for graph traversal\n- Fibonacci optimization examples\n\n**Behavioral:**\n- STAR method (Situation, Task, Action, Result) with detailed example\n\nEach question includes:\n- Comprehensive C# code examples\n- Performance analysis\n- Real-world use cases\n- When to use each approach\n- Common pitfalls to avoid\n\nTotal questions: 334 (167 per language)","tree":{"sha":"17751e9ee23c7ccb833692df89078e1fa01e1985","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/trees/17751e9ee23c7ccb833692df89078e1fa01e1985"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/commits/f0199d0d8fbefec7a559e5431fcc463e5e85dba6","verification":{"payload":"tree 17751e9ee23c7ccb833692df89078e1fa01e1985\nparent 96f57455710bdad9347d909f4a8c1496263a4884\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762476922 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762476922 +0000\n\nAdd 10 comprehensive interview questions from top GitHub resources\n\nSources analyzed:\n- awesome-behavioral-interviews (behavioral patterns)\n- master-coding-interview (data structures & algorithms)\n- tech-interview-handbook (interview best practices)\n- ztm-master-t