sers/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/commits/77b7855172d08ce50e5a8cf9009732545562a878/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-07T00:35:12Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-07T00:35:12Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add comprehensive interview categories and questions for Architect and Senior Developer positions\n\nCreated a detailed guide covering all major interview topics:\n\n**For Architect Position (12 categories, 120 questions):**\n1. Architecture Patterns & Systems (Monolith vs Microservices, Distributed Systems, Service Decomposition)\n2. Domain-Driven Design (Bounded Context, Aggregates, Domain Events, Strategic Design)\n3. Scalability & Performance (Horizontal/Vertical Scaling, Load Balancing, Caching, Sharding)\n4. Security (Authentication, Authorization, Zero Trust, OWASP Top 10, Encryption)\n5. Cloud & Infrastructure (AWS/Azure/GCP, Serverless, Kubernetes, IaC, DR Strategy)\n6. DevOps & CI/CD (Pipelines, GitOps, Deployment Strategies, Monitoring, SLA/SLO/SLI)\n7. Service Communication (REST, gRPC, GraphQL, Kafka, Service Discovery, Idempotency)\n8. Databases & Storage (SQL vs NoSQL, Polyglot Persistence, Sharding, Data Consistency)\n9. Observability & Reliability (Metrics/Logs/Traces, Distributed Tracing, SRE, Chaos Engineering)\n10. Team Management (Technical Leadership, ADR, Stakeholder Management, Mentoring)\n11. Architectural Trade-offs (Build vs Buy, Technology Selection, Risk Assessment)\n12. Legacy & Migrations (Strangler Fig, Modernization, Zero-Downtime Migration)\n\n**For Senior Developer Position (14 categories, 140 questions):**\n1. Advanced OOP (SOLID, Composition vs Inheritance, DI, IoC, Polymorphism)\n2. Design Patterns (Creational, Structural, Behavioral patterns with examples)\n3. Clean Code (Readability, Naming, DRY, Error Handling, Code Organization)\n4. Algorithms & Data Structures (Big O, Hash Tables, Trees, Graphs, Sorting)\n5. Performance & Optimization (Profiling, Memory Leaks, Caching, N+1 Problem)\n6. Testing (Test Pyramid, Unit/Integration/E2E, TDD, Mocking, BDD)\n7. Refactoring (Boy Scout Rule, Extract Method/Class, Legacy Code)\n8. Code Review & Collaboration (PR Best Practices, Git Workflow, Pair Programming)\n9. Frameworks & Libraries (Selection, Dependency Management, Security Updates)\n10. API Design (REST principles, Versioning, Pagination, Documentation)\n11. Databases (ORM vs Raw SQL, Indexing, Migrations, NoSQL, ACID)\n12. Git & Version Control (Branching Strategy, Merge vs Rebase, Git Hooks)\n13. Debugging & Troubleshooting (Tools, Production Debugging, Logging, Postmortems)\n14. Mentoring & Leadership (Teaching, Knowledge Transfer, Onboarding)\n\n**Additional Sections:**\n- Behavioral Questions (experience, collaboration, learning)\n- Coding/Design Challenges (practical tasks for interviews)\n- Questions for Candidates (what candidates should ask)\n\nTotal: 260+ questions covering all aspects of senior-level technical interviews","tree":{"sha":"5a598a846bd74fa0755fb36715ef0dccaaf931fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/trees/5a598a846bd74fa0755fb36715ef0dccaaf931fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/commits/77b7855172d08ce50e5a8cf9009732545562a878","verification":{"payload":"tree 5a598a846bd74fa0755fb36715ef0dccaaf931fe\nparent b3984db3a8570ff16bc1057d8c8f702d743dc34f\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762475712 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762475712 +0000\n\nAdd comprehensive interview categories and questions for Architect and Senior Developer positions\n\nCreated a detailed guide covering all major interview topics:\n\n**For Architect Position (12 categories, 120 questions):**\n1. Architecture Patterns & Systems (Monolith vs Microservices, Distributed Systems, Service Decomposition)\n2. Domain-Driven Design (Bounded Context, Aggregates, Domain Events, Strategic Design)\n3. Scalability & Performance (Horizontal/Vertical Scaling, Load Balancing, Caching, Sharding)\n4. Security (Authentication, Authorization, Zero Trust, OWASP Top 10, Encryption)\n5. Cloud & Infrastructure (AWS/Azure/GCP, Serverless, Kubernetes, IaC, DR Strategy)\n6. DevOps & CI/CD (Pipelines, GitOps, Deployment Strategies, Monitoring, SLA/SLO/SLI)\n7. Service Communication (REST, gRPC, GraphQL, Kafka, Service Discovery, Idempotency)\n8. Databases & Storage (SQL vs NoSQL, Polyglot Persistence, Sharding, Data Consistency)\n9. Observability & Reliability (Metrics/Logs/Traces, Distributed Tracing, SRE, Chaos Engineering)\n10. Team Management (Technical Leadership, ADR, Stakeholder Management, Mentoring)\n11. Architectural Trade-offs (Build vs Buy, Technology Selection, Risk Assessment)\n12. Legacy & Migrations (Strangler Fig, Modernization, Zero-Downtime Migration)\n\n**For Senior Developer Position (14 categories, 140 questions):**\n1. Advanced OOP (SOLID, Composition vs Inheritance, DI, IoC, Polymorphism)\n2. Design Patterns (Creational, Structural, Behavioral patterns with examples)\n3. Clean Code (Readability, Naming, DRY, Error Handling, Code Organization)\n4. Algorithms & Data Structures (Big O, Hash Tables, Trees, Graphs, Sorting)\n5. Performance & Optimization (Profiling, Memory Leaks, Caching, N+1 Problem)\n6. Testing (Test Pyramid, Unit/Integration/E2E, TDD, Mocking, BDD)\n7. Refactoring (Boy Scout Rule, Extract Method/Class, Legacy Code)\n8. Code Review & Collaboration (PR Best Practices, Git Workflow, Pair Programming)\n9. Frameworks & Libraries (Selection, Dependency Management, Security Updates)\n10. API Design (REST principles, Versioning, Pagination, Documentation)\n11. Databases (ORM vs Raw SQL, Indexing, Migrations, NoSQL, ACID)\n12. Git & Version Control (Branching Strategy, Merge vs Rebase, Git Hooks)\n13. Debugging & Troubleshooting (Tools, Production Debugging, Logging, Postmortems)\n14. Mentoring & Leadership (Teaching, Knowledge Transfer, Onboarding)\n\n**Additional Sections:**\n- Behavioral Questions (experience, collaboration, learning)\n- Coding/Design Challenges (practical tasks for interviews)\n- Questions for Candidates (what candidates should ask)\n\nTotal: 260+ questions covering all aspects of senior-level technical interviews\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLpH1rUx\n+hVsY/vtf9J27uMpIVx2i9ZZ8ZaWVvK4Hx1vptpuXf6ZK3mJoULZcBIwFznx3DcT+dEo6i6Lac5n\nLwk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-11-07T00:35:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users