claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/commits/b3984db3a8570ff16bc1057d8c8f702d743dc34f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-07T00:29:30Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-07T00:29:30Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add comprehensive Angular content across all experience levels\n\nAdded Angular interview questions and code examples for all three levels:\n\n**Mid-Level (programming-languages/mid-level.md):**\nSection 12: Angular Fundamentals (~800 lines)\n- Components: Structure, templates, lifecycle\n- Data Binding: Interpolation, property, event, two-way binding\n- Services & DI: Injectable services, HTTP requests, dependency injection\n- Directives: Structural (*ngIf, *ngFor, *ngSwitch) and Attribute (ngClass, ngStyle, custom directives)\n- Routing: Routes, parameters, navigation, RouterLink\n- Forms: Template-driven and reactive forms with validation\n- Pipes: Built-in pipes (date, currency, async) and custom pipes\n- Lifecycle Hooks: All 9 hooks with execution order\n- Input/Output: Parent-child component communication\n\n**Senior-Level (programming-languages/senior-level.md):**\nSection 7: Advanced Angular Concepts (~890 lines)\n- RxJS Operators: debounceTime, distinctUntilChanged, switchMap, combineLatest, forkJoin, BehaviorSubject\n- NgRx State Management: Actions, reducers, selectors, effects, complete store setup\n- Change Detection: Default vs OnPush strategies, performance optimization\n- Lazy Loading: Code splitting, preloading strategies, loadChildren\n- Route Guards: CanActivate, CanDeactivate, CanLoad, role-based access\n- Resolvers: Preload data before route activation\n- HTTP Interceptors: Auth token, error handling, loading indicators, caching\n- Content Projection: ng-content with multi-slot projection\n\n**Principal-Level (programming-languages/principal-level.md):**\nSection 5: Angular Enterprise Architecture (~770 lines)\n- Monorepo with Nx: Workspace structure, shared libraries, affected commands\n- Micro-Frontends: Module Federation, dynamic remotes, shared dependencies\n- Custom Schematics: Code generation, automated scaffolding\n- Performance at Scale: Build optimization, budgets, virtual scrolling, performance monitoring\n- Testing Strategy: Unit tests (Jest), component tests (MockStore), E2E tests (Cypress)\n- State Management Architecture: Facade pattern, clean separation of concerns\n- CI/CD Pipeline: GitHub Actions with Nx affected analysis\n\n**Total added:** ~2,460 lines of Angular content\n**Materials database:** Updated from 397KB → 459KB (+62KB)","tree":{"sha":"f691658ff4ea6ecffa1d4550d14f3657d31dfbb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/trees/f691658ff4ea6ecffa1d4550d14f3657d31dfbb4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/commits/b3984db3a8570ff16bc1057d8c8f702d743dc34f","verification":{"payload":"tree f691658ff4ea6ecffa1d4550d14f3657d31dfbb4\nparent 7ea1502b20d491971f6d5e6269fafaa5d92151b7\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762475370 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762475370 +0000\n\nAdd comprehensive Angular content across all experience levels\n\nAdded Angular interview questions and code examples for all three levels:\n\n**Mid-Level (programming-languages/mid-level.md):**\nSection 12: Angular Fundamentals (~800 lines)\n- Components: Structure, templates, lifecycle\n- Data Binding: Interpolation, property, event, two-way binding\n- Services & DI: Injectable services, HTTP requests, dependency injection\n- Directives: Structural (*ngIf, *ngFor, *ngSwitch) and Attribute (ngClass, ngStyle, custom directives)\n- Routing: Routes, parameters, navigation, RouterLink\n- Forms: Template-driven and reactive forms with validation\n- Pipes: Built-in pipes (date, currency, async) and custom pipes\n- Lifecycle Hooks: All 9 hooks with execution order\n- Input/Output: Parent-child component communication\n\n**Senior-Level (programming-languages/senior-level.md):**\nSection 7: Advanced Angular Concepts (~890 lines)\n- RxJS Operators: debounceTime, distinctUntilChanged, switchMap, combineLatest, forkJoin, BehaviorSubject\n- NgRx State Management: Actions, reducers, selectors, effects, complete store setup\n- Change Detection: Default vs OnPush strategies, performance optimization\n- Lazy Loading: Code splitting, preloading strategies, loadChildren\n- Route Guards: CanActivate, CanDeactivate, CanLoad, role-based access\n- Resolvers: Preload data before route activation\n- HTTP Interceptors: Auth token, error handling, loading indicators, caching\n- Content Projection: ng-content with multi-slot projection\n\n**Principal-Level (programming-languages/principal-level.md):**\nSection 5: Angular Enterprise Architecture (~770 lines)\n- Monorepo with Nx: Workspace structure, shared libraries, affected commands\n- Micro-Frontends: Module Federation, dynamic remotes, shared dependencies\n- Custom Schematics: Code generation, automated scaffolding\n- Performance at Scale: Build optimization, budgets, virtual scrolling, performance monitoring\n- Testing Strategy: Unit tests (Jest), component tests (MockStore), E2E tests (Cypress)\n- State Management Architecture: Facade pattern, clean separation of concerns\n- CI/CD Pipeline: GitHub Actions with Nx affected analysis\n\n**Total added:** ~2,460 lines of Angular content\n**Materials database:** Updated from 397KB → 459KB (+62KB)\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaG