/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/commits/bf8d7e78c2d084c51befbd110f23bb7679895328/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-07T00:24:05Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-07T00:24:05Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add Competitive Programming category with 15 C# coding challenges\n\nNew Category: Competitive Programming (C#)\n- Added brand new category focused on algorithmic coding challenges\n- All questions include complete C# code solutions\n- Covers classic competitive programming problems with optimal solutions\n\nQuestion Topics (15 questions × 2 languages = 30 total):\n\nMID LEVEL (5 questions):\n- Two Sum problem with HashSet - O(n) solution\n- Reverse linked list iteratively - O(1) space\n- Palindrome check with two pointers\n- Maximum subarray sum (Kadane''s algorithm)\n- Binary search with overflow prevention\n\nSENIOR LEVEL (10 questions):\n- Longest Increasing Subsequence - O(n log n) with binary search\n- Floyd''s Cycle Detection (tortoise & hare)\n- Trie (Prefix Tree) implementation\n- Merge K Sorted Lists with PriorityQueue\n- Knapsack 0/1 with space-optimized DP\n- String permutations with backtracking\n- Dijkstra''s shortest path algorithm\n- Lowest Common Ancestor in binary tree\n- Coin Change problem with DP\n- Union-Find with path compression\n\nFeatures:\n✓ Each question includes complete, production-ready C# code\n✓ Time and space complexity analysis\n✓ Detailed explanations of algorithms\n✓ Both Polish and English translations\n✓ Covers essential competitive programming patterns:\n  - Hash tables, two pointers, sliding window\n  - Dynamic programming (1D, 2D, space optimization)\n  - Graph algorithms (Dijkstra, Union-Find)\n  - Tree algorithms (DFS, LCA)\n  - Backtracking\n  - Advanced data structures (Trie, PriorityQueue)\n\nUpdated Statistics:\n- Total questions: 280 (was 250)\n- Questions per language: 140 (was 125)\n- Added: 30 new questions (+12% increase)\n- New categories: 8 (added Competitive Programming)\n\nAll code examples use modern C# syntax with nullable operators,\ntuple deconstruction, and .NET 6+ features.","tree":{"sha":"a83411996e4563207304a8559b9f238134956fb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/trees/a83411996e4563207304a8559b9f238134956fb4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/commits/bf8d7e78c2d084c51befbd110f23bb7679895328","verification":{"payload":"tree a83411996e4563207304a8559b9f238134956fb4\nparent b9db5a342a6a3e21bb61621afeb5fca4b19e5da8\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762475045 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762475045 +0000\n\nAdd Competitive Programming category with 15 C# coding challenges\n\nNew Category: Competitive Programming (C#)\n- Added brand new category focused on algorithmic coding challenges\n- All questions include complete C# code solutions\n- Covers classic competitive programming problems with optimal solutions\n\nQuestion Topics (15 questions × 2 languages = 30 total):\n\nMID LEVEL (5 questions):\n- Two Sum problem with HashSet - O(n) solution\n- Reverse linked list iteratively - O(1) space\n- Palindrome check with two pointers\n- Maximum subarray sum (Kadane''s algorithm)\n- Binary search with overflow prevention\n\nSENIOR LEVEL (10 questions):\n- Longest Increasing Subsequence - O(n log n) with binary search\n- Floyd''s Cycle Detection (tortoise & hare)\n- Trie (Prefix Tree) implementation\n- Merge K Sorted Lists with PriorityQueue\n- Knapsack 0/1 with space-optimized DP\n- String permutations with backtracking\n- Dijkstra''s shortest path algorithm\n- Lowest Common Ancestor in binary tree\n- Coin Change problem with DP\n- Union-Find with path compression\n\nFeatures:\n✓ Each question includes complete, production-ready C# code\n✓ Time and space complexity analysis\n✓ Detailed explanations of algorithms\n✓ Both Polish and English translations\n✓ Covers essential competitive programming patterns:\n  - Hash tables, two pointers, sliding window\n  - Dynamic programming (1D, 2D, space optimization)\n  - Graph algorithms (Dijkstra, Union-Find)\n  - Tree algorithms (DFS, LCA)\n  - Backtracking\n  - Advanced data structures (Trie, PriorityQueue)\n\nUpdated Statistics:\n- Total questions: 280 (was 250)\n- Questions per language: 140 (was 125)\n- Added: 30 new questions (+12% increase)\n- New categories: 8 (added Competitive Programming)\n\nAll code examples use modern C# syntax with nullable operators,\ntuple deconstruction, and .NET 6+ features.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ43UubS\nN6nGl09SHHLZqwdnkph9UQcHj40SZEJlAXnvN44a3pOhqO+F0m9hyHc44YLjVGcChVU9NWml2Myf\nqwI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-11-07T00:24:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gis