ubscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/commits/7ea1502b20d491971f6d5e6269fafaa5d92151b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-07T00:18:41Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-07T00:18:41Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add comprehensive interview questions for 6 new topics\n\nAdded detailed questions and multi-language code examples for:\n\n**Programming Languages (mid-level):**\n- SOLID Principles: All 5 principles with bad/good examples in C#, Python, JavaScript, TypeScript\n- OOP Basics: 4 pillars (Encapsulation, Inheritance, Polymorphism, Abstraction) with examples\n- React Fundamentals: Components, Props, State, Hooks (useState, useEffect, useContext, custom hooks)\n- jQuery Fundamentals: Selectors, DOM manipulation, events, AJAX, animations, comparison with vanilla JS\n- Performance Optimization: Time/space complexity, data structures, caching, async/parallel, profiling tools\n  - C# examples: LINQ performance, StringBuilder, HashSet vs List, async patterns, Span<T>, EF Core optimization, MemoryCache\n  - Python examples: Algorithm optimization, lru_cache, asyncio\n  - JavaScript examples: Debounce, throttle, virtual scrolling\n\n**Databases (mid-level):**\n- T-SQL Fundamentals: Stored procedures, functions (scalar, inline, multi-statement table-valued), CTEs (simple, recursive)\n  - Window functions: ROW_NUMBER, RANK, DENSE_RANK, LAG/LEAD, running totals\n  - Transactions with TRY/CATCH, temp tables vs table variables, dynamic SQL\n  - C# implementations using ADO.NET, Dapper, Entity Framework Core\n  - T-SQL vs Standard SQL comparison table\n\n**Total added:** ~2,100 lines of new content across both files\n**Regenerated:** materials-data.js (320KB → 397KB) to include all new content","tree":{"sha":"10cfe1624ce5de1926286edb5ce8d0666912