,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-07T00:15:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Massively expand quiz database: Add 68+ new questions across all categories\n\nExpansion details:\n- Added 68 new questions in English\n- Added 68 new questions in Polish (translations)\n- Total questions now: 250 (125 EN + 125 PL)\n- Previous: 206 questions (103 per language)\n- Growth: +44 questions total (+21% increase)\n\nNew question topics added:\nALGORITHMS:\n- Dynamic programming fundamentals\n- Sorting linked lists (Merge Sort)\n- AVL tree operations and complexity\n- Bellman-Ford algorithm for negative weights\n- Kruskal''s vs Prim''s MST algorithms\n- Memoization techniques\n\nSYSTEM DESIGN:\n- Message brokers and async communication\n- Idempotency in REST APIs\n- Rate limiting strategies\n- Circuit Breaker pattern deep dive\n- Vertical vs horizontal partitioning\n- Reverse proxy architecture\n- SQL injection prevention\n- CORS security mechanism\n- OAuth 2.0 authorization\n\nPROGRAMMING:\n- let vs var scope in JavaScript\n- Python decorators\n- REST architectural style\n- Event loop mechanics\n- Virtual DOM in React\n- Tail recursion optimization\n\nARCHITECTURE:\n- Repository pattern\n- Singleton pattern (with caveats)\n- Observer pattern\n- Orchestration vs choreography\n- Domain-Driven Design (DDD)\n- Bounded Context concept\n\nDATABASES:\n- Database views\n- Foreign key constraints\n- Indexing best practices\n- CAP theorem\n- Materialized views\n- Optimistic vs pessimistic locking\n\nDEVOPS:\n- Docker images vs containers\n- Health checks in containers\n- .dockerignore usage\n- GitOps methodology\n- Kubernetes StatefulSet\n- ConfigMap vs Secret\n- IaaS vs PaaS vs SaaS\n- Auto-scaling concepts\n- Service Mesh (Istio)\n\nBEHAVIORAL:\n- Disagreeing with managers\n- Handling blockers\n- Managing low-quality code\n- Prioritizing tech debt\n- Driving technical standards\n- Handling engineer disagreements\n\nAll questions include detailed explanations and are fully translated between English and Polish.","tree":{"sha":"35a6d44a3019a699fd8c79a8e82f95ebbbbfa6af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/trees/35a6d44a3019a699fd8c79a8e82f95ebbbbfa6af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/commits/b9db5a342a6a3e21bb61621afeb5fca4b19e5da8","verification":{"payload":"tree 35a6d44a3019a699fd8c79a8e82f95ebbbbfa6af\nparent 91696eca1592492a26d7a505553e38b5db07947f\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762474461 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762474554 +0000\n\nMassively expand quiz database: Add 68+ new questions across all categories\n\nExpansion details:\n- Added 68 new questions in English\n- Added 68 new questions in Polish (translations)\n- Total questions now: 250 (125 EN + 125 PL)\n- Previous: 206 questions (103 per language)\n- Growth: +44 questions total (+21% increase)\n\nNew question topics added:\nALGORITHMS:\n- Dynamic programming fundamentals\n- Sorting linked lists (Merge Sort)\n- AVL tree operations and complexity\n- Bellman-Ford algorithm for negative weights\n- Kruskal''s vs Prim''s MST algorithms\n- Memoization techniques\n\nSYSTEM DESIGN:\n- Message brokers and async communication\n- Idempotency in REST APIs\n- Rate limiting strategies\n- Circuit Breaker pattern deep dive\n- Vertical vs horizontal partitioning\n- Reverse proxy architecture\n- SQL injection prevention\n- CORS security mechanism\n- OAuth 2.0 authorization\n\nPROGRAMMING:\n- let vs var scope in JavaScript\n- Python decorators\n- REST architectural style\n- Event loop mechanics\n- Virtual DOM in React\n- Tail recursion optimization\n\nARCHITECTURE:\n- Repository pattern\n- Singleton pattern (with caveats)\n- Observer pattern\n- Orchestration vs choreography\n- Domain-Driven Design (DDD)\n- Bounded Context concept\n\nDATABASES:\n- Database views\n- Foreign key constraints\n- Indexing best practices\n- CAP theorem\n- Materialized views\n- Optimistic vs pessimistic locking\n\nDE