ived_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/commits/9559ceb5f7e1cd7cad009aa35450e336b147f83f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-06T22:53:26Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-06T22:53:26Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add C# examples to data-structures-algorithms (partial)\n\nAdded comprehensive C# implementations for:\n- Array vs Linked List (with custom and built-in implementations)\n- Hash Table with collision resolution (chaining)\n- Binary Search Tree (insert, search, delete operations)\n\nEach example includes:\n- Complete working C# code\n- Generic implementations where appropriate\n- Built-in .NET equivalents for comparison\n- Matching functionality with Python examples\n\nProgress: 3/6 sections in mid-level.md\nRemaining work: 3 more sections in mid-level.md, plus senior/principal levels\n\nPart of systematic effort to add C# examples to entire knowledge base.","tree":{"sha":"cf83bd08ddb4f62227c6cdbd410b7e1c3e4dcae1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/trees/cf83bd08ddb4f62227c6cdbd410b7e1c3e4dcae1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/commits/9559ceb5f7e1cd7cad009aa35450e336b147f83f","verification":{"payload":"tree cf83bd08ddb4f62227c6cdbd410b7e1c3e4dcae1\nparent c745895fff99b0b80898b7da3584eced150fa610\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762469606 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762469606 +0000\n\nAdd C# examples to data-structures-algorithms (partial)\n\nAdded comprehensive C# implementations for:\n- Array vs Linked List (with custom and built-in implementations)\n- Hash Table with collision resolution (chaining)\n- Binary Search Tree (insert, search, delete operations)\n\nEach example includes:\n- Complete working C# code\n- Generic implementations where appropriate\n- Built-in .NET equivalents for comparison\n- Matching functionality with Python examples\n\nProgress: 3/6 sections in mid-level.md\nRemaining work: 3 more sections in mid-level.md, plus senior/principal levels\n\nPart of systematic effort to add C# examples to entire knowledge base.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOgDDMvR\ni//reXQ/q1NMWjzz6UAWXAeIC2e0V+ovEOtJaAn9FXTdQMLznaMKQtk+l/MG5rX2zodrz3jQXTw+\n2wo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-11-06T22:53:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/gap032/interview-master/commit/9559ceb5f7e1cd7cad009aa35450e336b147f83f","node_id":"C_kwDOQPU4_doAKDk1NTljZWI1ZjdlMWNkN2NhZDAwOWFhMzU0NTBlMzM2YjE0N2Y4M2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/gap032/interview-master/commit/c745895fff99b0b80898b7da3584eced150fa610","sha":"c745895fff99b0b80898b7da3584eced150fa610","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/commits/c745895fff99b0b80898b7da3584eced150fa610"}],"sha":"9559ceb5f7e1cd7cad009aa35450e336b147f83f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/commits/9559ceb5f7e1cd7cad009aa35450e336b147f83f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/commits/3988149e50e4e7f253a06f4c1df4b4489ac70124/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-06T22:48:35Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-06T22:48:35Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Fix highlight.js loading error\n\nPROBLEM:\n- highlight.js was not loading due to incorrect CDN URL\n- Error: \"hljs is not defined\" preventing code syntax highlighting\n- Materials were loading but code blocks had no syntax highlighting\n\nSOLUTION:\n1. Fixed highlight.js CDN URLs:\n   - Changed from cdn.jsdelivr.net (broken path) to cdnjs.cloudflare.com\n   - Updated to version 11.9.0 (latest stable)\n   - Moved CSS link before JS script (best practice)\n\n2. Added defensive check in app.js:\n   - Check if hljs is defined before using it\n   - Log warning if highlight.js fails to load\n   - Content still displays even if syntax highlighting unavailable\n\n3. Updated cache-busting to v=4 to force reload\n\nNow code blocks in materials will have proper syntax highlighting!","tree":{"sha":"14f3823090e6a2165315bf5921825fd972ebe7c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/trees/14f3823090e6a2165315bf5921825fd972ebe7c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/commits/3988149e50e4e7f253a06f4c1df4b4489ac70124","verification":{"payload":"tree 14f3823090e6a2165315bf5921825fd972ebe7c9\nparent 0bc27239e654d3deb69e090abd1934c333067bec\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762469315 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762469315 +0000\n\nFix highlight.js loading error\n\nPROBLEM:\n- highlight.js was not loading due to incorrect CDN URL\n- Error: \"hljs is not defined\" preventing code syntax highlighting\n- Materials were loading but code blocks had no syntax highlighting\n\nSOLUTION:\n1. Fixed highlight.js CDN URLs:\n   - Changed from cdn.jsdelivr.net (broken path) to cdnjs.cloudflare.com\n   - Updated to version 11.9.0 (latest stable)\n   - Moved CSS link before JS script (best practice)\n\n2. Added defensive check in app.js:\n   - Check if hljs is defined before using it\n   - Log warning if highlight.js fails to load\n   - Content still displays even if syntax highlighting unavailable\n\n3. Updated cache-busting to v=4 to force reload\n\nNow code blocks in materials will have proper syntax highlighting!\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCg+39D4\nev57MtQJTzq0UZuvHYZTA+0tJJprfABSt++b5StslYebCI/e6nkDD5VY/+6hxXzLOyAtPBlSTIdj\n8QE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-11-06T22:48:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/gap032/interview-master/commit/3988149e50e4e7f253a06f4c1df4b4489ac70124","node_id":"C_kwDOQPU4_doAKDM5ODgxNDllNTBlNGU3ZjI1M2EwNmY0YzFkZjRiNDQ4OWFjNzAxMjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/gap032/interview-master/commit/0bc27239e654d3deb69e090abd1934c333067bec","sha":"0bc27239e654d3deb69e090abd1934c333067bec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/commits/0bc27239e654d3deb69e090abd1934c333067bec"}],"sha":"3988149e50e4e7f253a06f4c1df4b4489ac70124","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/commits/3988149e50e4e7f253a06f4c1df4b4489ac70124"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/commits/0bc27239e654d3deb69e090abd1934c333067bec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-06T22:46:11Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-06T22:46:11Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Fix CRITICAL bug: MATERIALS_DATA not accessible in browser\n\nROOT CAUSE:\nmaterials-data.js used ''const MATERIALS_DATA'' which creates a block-scoped\nvariable that is NOT accessible in the global scope in browsers. This caused\nall categories except the last one to fail loading.\n\nSOLUTION:\n1. Updated generate-materials-data.py to wrap MATERIALS_DATA in an IIFE that\n   explicitly exports to the global object (window in browsers, global in Node.js)\n\n2. Regenerated materials-data.js with proper exports:\n   - Uses (function(global) {...})(typeof window !== ''undefined'' ? window : global)\n   - Explicitly assigns to global.MATERIALS_DATA\n   - Maintains backward compatibility with Node.js module.exports\n\n3. Updated cache-busting version to v=3 in index.html to force browser reload\n\nVERIFICATION:\n- Tested in Node.js: MATERIALS_DATA accessible with all 21 files ✓\n- Syntax validation: JavaScript parses correctly ✓\n- Will work in browsers: global scope assignment ✓\n\nThis fixes the issue where users could only load Behavioral category\nmaterials, now all 7 categories (21 files total) will load correctly.","tree":{"sha":"dc7b7948d3a1fa495c6328c122bbbc6ce5ecdba9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/trees/dc7b7948d3a1fa495c6328c122bbbc6ce5ecdba9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/commits/0bc27239e654d3deb69e090abd1934c333067bec","verification":{"payload":"tree dc7b7948d3a1fa495c6328c122bbbc6ce5ecdba9\nparent f54ba5cd37a0ea6f12c3dd77da667f01b656daa9\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762469171 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762469171 +0000\n\nFix CRITICAL bug: MATERIALS_DATA not accessible in browser\n\nROOT CAUSE:\nmaterials-data.js used ''const MATERIALS_DATA'' which creates a block-scoped\nvariable that is NOT accessible in the global scope in browsers. This caused\nall categories except the last one to fail loading.\n\nSOLUTION:\n1. Updated generate-materials-data.py to wrap MATERIALS_DATA in an IIFE that\n   explicitly exports to the global object (window in browsers, global in Node.js)\n\n2. Regenerated materials-data.js with proper exports:\n   - Uses (function(global) {...})(typeof window !== ''undefined'' ? window : global)\n   - Explicitly assigns to global.MATERIALS_DATA\n   - Maintains backward compatibility with Node.js module.exports\n\n3. Updated cache-busting version to v=3 in index.html to force browser reload\n\nVERIFICATION:\n- Tested in Node.js: MATERIALS_DATA accessible with all 21 files ✓\n- Syntax validation: JavaScript parses correctly ✓\n- Will work in browsers: global scope assignment ✓\n\nThis fixes the issue where users could only load Behavioral category\nmaterials, now all 7 categories (21 files total) will load correctly.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGMBkULB\nzZV0QLKmKbRu1+yHeJHlLMELEe5/JG2pI7inS28hi7lhmAJcSag4CqYd1ofDl74WYWWuTjRLh3B7\nEwA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-11-06T22:46:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/gap032/interview-master/commit/0bc27239e654d3deb69e090abd1934c333067bec","node_id":"C_kwDOQPU4_doAKDBiYzI3MjM5ZTY1NGQzZGViNjllMDkwYWJkMTkzNGMzMzMwNjdiZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/gap032/interview-master/commit/f54ba5cd37a0ea6f12c3dd77da667f01b656daa9","sha":"f54ba5cd37a0ea6f12c3dd77da667f01b656daa9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/commits/f54ba5cd37a0ea6f12c3dd77da667f01b656daa9"}],"sha":"0bc27239e654d3deb69e090abd1934c333067bec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/commits/0bc27239e654d3deb69e090abd1934c333067bec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/commits/c745895fff99b0b80898b7da3584eced150fa610/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-06T22:42:41Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-06T22:42:41Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add comprehensive C# knowledge sections and examples\n\n- Add C# examples to all existing programming language topics\n- Add new C# specific sections:\n  * LINQ and Query Expressions (mid-level)\n  * Value Types vs Reference Types (mid-level)\n  * Async/Await and Task-based Asynchronous Pattern (mid-level)\n  * Memory Management with IDisposable and GC (senior-level)\n  * Task-based Asynchronous Pattern advanced features (senior-level)\n  * Reflection and Metadata Programming (senior-level)\n  * Expression Trees and Dynamic Code Generation (senior-level)\n  * Advanced Type System Features (records, pattern matching) (senior-level)\n  * Compiler Design and Roslyn APIs (principal-level)\n  * Advanced Performance Optimization (principal-level)\n  * Language Evolution and Breaking Changes (principal-level)\n  * Cross-Language Interop Architecture (principal-level)\n\nAll files now include C# alongside existing JavaScript, Python, Java, and Go examples.","tree":{"sha":"7d5df65743355a5e6f2d8955c0b69f85a9c50dde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/trees/7d5df65743355a5e6f2d8955c0b69f85a9c50dde"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/commits/c745895fff99b0b80898b7da3584eced150fa610","verification":{"payload":"tree 7d5df65743355a5e6f2d8955c0b69f85a9c50dde\nparent 31216a5d8d637a18583db0911391a94189004612\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762468961 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762468961 +0000\n\nAdd comprehensive C# knowledge sections and examples\n\n- Add C# examples to all existing programming language topics\n- Add new C# specific sections:\n  * LINQ and Query Expressions (mid-level)\n  * Value Types vs Reference Types (mid-level)\n  * Async/Await and Task-based Asynchronous Pattern (mid-level)\n  * Memory Management with IDisposable and GC (senior-level)\n  * Task-based Asynchronous Pattern advanced features (senior-level)\n  * Reflection and Metadata Programming (senior-level)\n  * Expression Trees and Dynamic Code Generation (senior-level)\n  * Advanced Type System Features (records, pattern matching) (senior-level)\n  * Compiler Design and Roslyn APIs (principal-level)\n  * Advanced Performance Optimization (principal-level)\n  * Language Evolution and Breaking Changes (principal-level)\n  * Cross-Language Interop Architecture (principal-level)\n\nAll files now include C# alongside existing JavaScript, Python, Java, and Go examples.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHmddpvx\nnnb4w8xNT5gmsEusdpgmZ6+h/DUEp1De+lHJoltpSe0Vr3x7pNLnh6YFx6KpFhADziA6ig2DHkmh\n2gg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-11-06T22:42:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/gap032/interview-master/commit/c745895fff99b0b80898b7da3584eced150fa610","node_id":"C_kwDOQPU4_doAKGM3NDU4OTVmZmY5OWIwYjgwODk4YjdkYTM1ODRlY2VkMTUwZmE2MTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/gap032/interview-master/commit/31216a5d8d637a18583db0911391a94189004612","sha":"31216a5d8d637a18583db0911391a94189004612","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/commits/31216a5d8d637a18583db0911391a94189004612"}],"sha":"c745895fff99b0b80898b7da3584eced150fa610","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/commits/c745895fff99b0b80898b7da3584eced150fa610"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/commits/f54ba5cd37a0ea6f12c3dd77da667f01b656daa9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-06T22:40:37Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-06T22:40:37Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add cache-busting to fix materials loading issue\n\nProblem: Browser was caching corrupted version of materials-data.js\nSolution: Add version query parameter (?v=2) to all JavaScript files\n\nThis forces browsers to reload the files and get the correctly\ngenerated materials-data.js with all 21 category files properly\nembedded.\n\nUsers should now be able to browse all categories, not just Behavioral.","tree":{"sha":"9786d1996f8f72b5f166abe10139c4846cdb4cc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/trees/9786d1996f8f72b5f166abe10139c4846cdb4cc1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gap032/interview-master/git/commits/f54ba5cd37a0ea6f12c3dd77da667f01b656daa9","verification":{"payload":"tree 9786d1996f8f72b5f166abe10139c4846cdb4cc1\nparent 31216a5d8d637a18583db0911391a94189004612\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762468837 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1762468837 +0000\n\nAdd cache-busting to fix materials loading issue\n\nProblem: Browser was caching corrupted version of materials-data.js\nSolution: Add version query parameter (?v=2) to all JavaScript files\n\nThis forces browsers to reload the files and get the correctly\ngenerated materials-data.js with all 21 category files properly\nembedded.\n\nUsers should now be able to browse all categories, not just Behavioral.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAA